license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Explainable-AI-Berlin/pytorch_explain_and_adapt_library"
abstract: >-
  PEAL is a PyTorch library for generating visual counterfactual explanations and for
  correcting classifiers and foundation-model probes with them. It contains the official
  implementations of Smoothed Counterfactual Explorer (SCE), Counterfactual Knowledge
  Distillation (CFKD) and Disentangled Diffusion Autoencoders (DiDAE), alongside
  reimplementations of commonly used counterfactual explainers and robustification methods.
keywords:
  - explainable AI
  - counterfactual explanations
  - spurious correlations
  - diffusion models
  - sparse autoencoders
